# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Moved from an inline build.sh
# --check block by the .step series (batch 4: the next slowest blocks,
# measured one at a time on lenovinha). As a .step it is no build.sh edit, so it
# never makes intake HEAVY; it runs in the pool (it writes only its own scratch).
#
# ORDER 1384-bxhk — the shell ratchet: prints the Lua migration's counts on
# every --check, refuses a NEW .sh decider (check-/test-/verify-/guard-), a
# new pipe site beyond a file's floor and (once steps: exists) a new piped
# litmus command; its floors only descend over their own git history.
STEP_DESC="Checking the shell ratchet (1384-bxhk)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/check-shell-ratchet.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the shell corpus grew past its floor — see the violation lines above; write it as scripts/lua/<name>.lua on tillandsias-plan script run (1384-bxhk)"
STEP_OK="Shell ratchet passed"
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/check-shell-ratchet.lua"
